    "text": "### 1.2 l 63/77 kW TSI engine with turbocharger\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\ns511_116\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nThe 1.2 l TSI engine from the new EA211 petrol engine family is available in two different power versions with 63 kW or 77 kW. The two different power versions is achieved via the software.\n\n##### Technical features\n\n- Cylinder head with integrated exhaust manifold \n\n- Camshafts driven by a toothed belt \n\n- The thermostat housing and the coolant pump form a single unit \n\n- Coolant pump driven by a toothed belt from the exhaust camshaft \n\n\n\n- Turbocharger with electric charge pressure positioner \n\n- Inlet camshaft adjustment \n\n- Crankshaft oil pump \n\n- Two-section sump \n\n   - (upper and lower section made of aluminium) \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\n(upper and lower section made of aluminium) Technical data\nEngine code CJZB CJZA\nTorque and performance diagram Design 4-cylinder inline engine\n[Nm] [kW] Displacement 1197 cm 3\nBore 71 mm\n220 80 Stroke 75.6 mm\nCompression ratio 10.5:1\n180 60\nMax. output 63 kW at 77 kW at\n4300 - 5300 4500 - 5500\n160 50\nrpm rpm\nMax. torque 160 Nm at 175 Nm at\n140 40\n1400 - 3500 1400 - 4000\nrpm rpm\n120 30\nEngine management Bosch Motronic MED 17.5.21\n100 20 Fuel Super unleaded with RON 95\nExhaust gas Three-way catalytic converter\n1000 2000 3000 4000 5000 6000 [rpm] aftertreatment with one step-type Lambda\nprobe before and one after the\nCJZB 63 kW catalytic converter\nCJZA 77 kW Emissions standard EU5\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n##### Torque and performance diagram\n\n7\n\nIntroduction",
