    "text": "### 1.4 l 90 kW TSI engine with turbocharger\n\nThe 1.4 l 90 kW TSI engine is hardly distinguishable from the 1.4 l 103 kW TSI engine on the outside. However, while both power versions feature inlet camshaft adjustment, the 103 kW version features additional exhaust camshaft adjustment. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\ns511_117\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n##### Technical features\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\n• Cylinder head with integrated exhaust manifold • Turbocharger with electric charge pressure\n• Camshafts driven by a toothed belt positioner\n• The thermostat housing and the coolant pump • Inlet camshaft adjustment\nform a single unit • External gear wheel oil pump with two-stage oil\n• Coolant pump driven by a toothed belt from the pressure regulation\nexhaust camshaft • Two-section sump\n(upper section made of aluminium, lower section\nmade of sheet metal)\nTorque and performance diagram Technical data\n[Nm] [kW]\n260 100 Engine code CMBA\nDesign 4-cylinder inline engine\n240 90\nDisplacement 1395 cm 3\n220 80 Bore 74.5 mm\nStroke 80 mm\n180 60\nCompression ratio 10.5:1\n160 50 Max. output 90 kW at 5000 - 6000 rpm\nMax. torque 200 Nm at\n140 40 1400 - 4000 rpm\n120 30 Engine management Bosch Motronic MED 17.5.21\nFuel Super unleaded with RON 95\n100 20\nExhaust gas Three-way catalytic converter\naftertreatment with one step-type Lambda\n1000 2000 3000 4000 5000 6000 [rpm] probe before and one after the\ncatalytic converter\nEmissions standard EU5\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n8",
