    "text": "## Cylinder block\n\nThe cylinder block consists of cast aluminium and has been designed as an open-deck version. Open deck means that it has no webs between the outer wall of the cylinder block and the cylinder liners. \n\n\n\nThe has the advantage of: \n\n- not allowing air bubbles to form in this area, which would lead to ventilation and cooling problems \n\ncylinder deformation is kept low when the cylinder head is bolted to the cylinder block. The piston rings can easily compensate this low level of cylinder liner deformation, and the consumption of oil is reduced. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nThe galleries for the oil pressure supply, the oil return pipes and the crankcase breather have been cast into the\ncylinder block. This reduces the number of additional components as well as the amount of machining required.\nCylinder liners Cylinder barrel\nOil return\nDuct for internal\ncrankcase breather\nCylinder block\nUntreated\ncast surface\ns511_015\nOil supply Crankcase breather\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n##### Grey cast iron cylinder liners\n\nThe grey cast iron cylinder liners are individually cast into the cylinder block. Their outer surface is very coarse, which increases the surface area and improves the transfer of heat to the cylinder block. \n\nIn addition, this ensures that there is a firm fit between the cylinder block and the cylinder liner. \n\n14",
