    "text": "### External gear oil pump\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nAn external gear oil pump is being used in the 1.4 l Crankshaft\nTSI engines. It features very efficient operation and\ncontributes to fuel savings and CO2 reductions.\nThe oil pump is bolted onto the upper section of the\nsump and operates in two pressure stages of approx.\n1.8 bar and 3.3 bar depending on the load and\nengine speed.\nIt is driven by the crankshaft via a maintenance-free\nchain drive without a chain tensioner.\nThe respective oil pressure is regulated by the oil\nquantity pumped.\nSump (upper\nsection)\nOil pump Chain drive\nSump (bottom\nsection)\nDriven by crankshaft\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n##### Advantages of the two-level oil pressure and oil quantity regulation\n\n- The drive output of the oil pump is lowered because the oil pump only pumps as much oil as is required. \n\n- Oil degradation is reduced, because less oil is being circulated. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\n[bar]\n3.5\n3.3\n1.8\ns511_202\napprox. 1400 rpm 4000 rpm\n150 Nm\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nPressure requirements Oil pressure unregulated (1.0 l and 1.2 l engines) Oil pressure regulated in two levels (1.4 l engines) Low pressure stage High pressure stage \n\n26",
