    "text": "#### External gear oil pump\n\nThe housing and the housing cover are made of aluminium and feature several control ports for oil pressure regulation. Depending on how the control piston and the slide unit are pressurised with oil from the oil circuit via the control ports, the quantity of oil being pumped and the oil pressure will change. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nOil strainer Control ports\noutlet\nDrive wheel oil pump Slide unit\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n\n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nThe control piston and the slide unit Position of slide unit at max. oil delivery quantity\nControl ports\nThe oil is actually pumped by two intermeshed gear\nControl piston\nwheels (pump gears).\nOne pump gear is located on the drive shaft, which is\ndriven by the crankshaft via a chain. Pump wheel\nThe second pump gear is located on a shaft which\ncan be moved longitudinally. The pump gear and the\nshaft form the slide unit.\ns511_247\nThe slide unit allows an influence to be exerted on the\ndelivery rate and the delivery pressure in the oil Slide unit with\npump gear\ncircuit.\nThe position of the slide unit is determined by the Position of slide unit at min. oil delivery quantity\npressure ratio acting in the chambers to the left and\nright of the slide unit.\nThe pressure ratio depends, in turn, on the activation\nof the control piston.\nPump wheel\ns511_248\nChamber Slide unit with\npump gear\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n27\n\nEngine mechanics",
