    "text": "#### Valve for oil pressure control N428\n\nThe valve for oil pressure control is actuated by an earth signal from the engine control unit in accordance with the load and engine speed. A valve is used to switch between the two oil pressure stages by alternately supplying the various control ports of the oil pump with oil. \n\nThe valve features the following switch states: \n\n- If the valve is actuated, it opens the control port to the oil pump and pumps at the low oil pressure stage of 1.8 bar. \n\n- If the valve is not actuated, the port is kept closed by spring pressure and the oil pump and pumps at the high oil pressure stage of 3.3 bar. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\ns511_177\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nValve for oil pressure control N428",
