    "page_end": 30,
    "text": "### The oil pressure control\n\nCompared to an unregulated oil pump, the drive power had already been reduced considerably in the regulated ducocentric oil pumps in the EA111 petrol engine family. It only pumped as much oil over the entire engine speed range as was needed to keep the oil pressure at a constant 3.5 bar. \n\nWith the new oil pumps for the EA211 engine family, the oil pressure is regulated at two levels depending on the engine speed and load. Above all, in the lower to medium engine speed/load range, the drive power falls as the oil pressure is only approx. 1.8 bar in this case. Less oil therefore has to be pumped by the oil pump. \n\n\n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nExhaust camshaft control valve 1 N318 Camshaft control valve 1 N205\nExhaust camshaft adjuster Inlet camshaft adjuster\nLubrication points for camshafts, Fourfold cams\nhydraulic compensation elements and\nvalves\nFuel pressure\nregulator\nOil pressure switch for reduced oil\npressure F378\nPiston cooling\nOil pressure switch F1 Lubrication point for crankshaft\nValve for oil pressure\ncontrol N428\nOil cooler\nExternal gear oil pump\nOil pump drive\nReturn\nOil filter\nSump\nIntake fitting\ns511_180\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n29\n\nEngine mechanics",
