    "text": "## Crankcase breather and ventilation system\n\nThe crankcase breather and ventilation system must ensure that: \n\n\n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nThe formation of condensation in the oil remains low on short trips and therefore prevents the crankcase\nbreather from freezing, and\noil vapour and uncombusted hydrocarbons are prevented from being emitted into the environment under all\noperating conditions.\nCrankcase breather\nThe crankcase breather allows the crankcase to be\nflushed with fresh air, therefore reducing the\nformation of condensation in the oil. It is ventilated\nwith fresh air using a hose leading from the air filter Connection on the air\nto the non-return valve on the camshaft housing. filter\nThe non-return valve prevents oil or unfiltered blow- s511_234\nby gases from entering the air filter. If the pressure in\nthe crankcase becomes too high, it opens the path to\nthe air filter. This prevents any damage to seals due\nto excessive pressures.\ns511_235\n<!-- End of picture text -->",
