    "text": "### Charge pressure sender G31 and intake air temperature sender G42\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nThe charge pressure sender with intake air s511_206\ntemperature sender is screwed into the pressure pipe\njust in front of the throttle valve module. It measures\nthe pressure and temperature in this area.\nSignal use\nThe engine control unit regulates the turbocharger\ncharge pressure using the signal from the charge\nCharge pressure sender G31 and\npressure sender. It is regulated via the electrical\nintake air temperature sender G42\ncharge pressure positioner.\nThe signal from the intake air temperature sender is\nrequired:\nto protect components. If the temperature of the Effects upon signal failure\ncharge air rises above a certain value, the charge If one or both senders fail, the turbocharger\npressure is reduced. operation is just regulated.\nThe charge pressure is lower and the power is\nThe signals from both intake air temperature senders reduced.\nG42 and G299 are required:\nto activate the charge air cooling pump. If the\ntemperature difference of the charge air before\nand after the charge air cooler is less than 12 °C,\nthe charge air cooling pump is activated. If it\nincreases to more than 15 °C, the pump is\ndeactivated again.\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n\n\n- for a plausibility test of the charge air cooling system. If, under certain conditions, the temperature difference between the charge air before and after the charge air cooler is too low despite activation of the charge air cooling pump, then it is assumed there is a fault in the charge air cooling system. \n\n47\n\nEngine management system",
