    "text": "#### Toothed belt for the coolant pump\n\nBefore removing the drive wheel, and when tensioning the toothed belt, you must pay attention to the notes in ELSA. Only a correctly tensioned toothed belt will ensure the coolant pump functions long-term without fail. \n\nTo ensure the toothed belt for the coolant pump is correctly tensioned, it must be pretensioned to an exact torque via the thermostat housing using the electronic torque wrench VAS 6583. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nCamshaft Exhaust\ndrive gear camshaft\nToothed belt\nCoolant\ndrive gear s511_258\n<!-- End of picture text -->",
