    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 21,
    "text": "## **Integral exhaust manifold**\n\nA cooled exhaust manifold with cylinder sequence separation is directly integrated with the cylinder head. \n\nThe use of this manifold significantly lowers the exhaust temperature upstream of the turbine when compared to a conventional manifold layout.  In addition, a highly heat resistant turbocharger is used. \n\nBecause of the new manifold design, there is no longer a need for full throttle mixture enrichment to protect the turbocharger turbine during high speed engine operation. This improves fuel economy during normal operation and when driving in a more aggressive, sporty manner. \n\nThe integral exhaust manifold facilitates rapid coolant heating and therefore, is a key part of the thermal management system.",
