    "text": "#### **Piston cooling jet control**\n\nThe piston cooling jets are activated only when required. This calculation is made on the basis of a special map stored in the engine control module \n\nThe key calculation factors are: \n\n- Engine load \n\n- Engine speed \n\nThe piston cooling jets can be activated both in the low and high pressure stages. \n\n- Calculated oil temperature \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\n258 lb ft\n221 lb ft\n184 lb ft\n147 lb ft\n110 lb ft\n74 lb ft\n37 lb ft\nTorque\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nPiston cooling switched off - oil temperature < 122 °F (50 °C) \n\nPiston cooling switched off - oil temperature > 122 °F (50 °C) \n\n606_019 \n\n32",
