    "text": "### **Engine Temperature Control Actuator N493 (rotary slide valve)**\n\nEngine Temperature Control Actuator N493 is identical for longitudinally and transversely mounted engines. It regulates coolant flow by means of two mechanically coupled rotary slide valves. The angular position of the rotary slide valves is regulated according to various maps stored in the ECM. \n\nVarious switching positions can be implemented by configuring the rotary slide valves accordingly. This allows rapid heating of the engine, which, in turn, results in lower friction and improved fuel economy. In addition, variable engine operating temperatures between 185 °F - 225 °F (85 °C - 107 °C) are possible. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\n1 2 3 4 5\n6\n7 10 11\n606_036\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n##### **Key:**\n\n- **1** N493 with sender \n\n- **2** Connecting piece for radiator supply line \n\n- **3** Connecting piece to lube oil cooler connection \n\n- **4** Idler gear **5** Rotary slide valve 2 \n\n- **6** Shaft for rotary slide valve 1 **7** Rotary slide valve housing **8** Expanding element thermostat (fail-safe thermostat) **9** Sealing package \n\n- **10** Connecting piece for return line from radiator **11** Rotary slide valve 1 \n\n38",
