    "text": "#### **Temperature regulation sequence**\n\n- During warm-up, the engine runs through three phases: \n\n- Static coolant \n\n- Mini-volume stream \n\n- Enable engine oil cooler \n\nThe different phases are accomplished through the positions of the rotary valves. The objective is to use the energy generated by the fuel combustion to heat the engine as much as possible. However, if passenger compartment heating is required during the \"static coolant\" phase, heat energy is provided to the interior. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nNon-return valves\nCylinder head with\nintegrated exhaust\nmanifold Passenger compart-\nment heat exchanger\nAfter-run Coolant\nPump V51\nClimatronic Coolant\nEngine oil cooler Shut-off Valve N422\nRotary valve 1 Coolant pump\nEngine Temperature\nControl Actuator\nEmergency mode Main radiator N493\nthermostat\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\ns522_092 \n\n41",
