    "text": "#### **Warm-up with mini-volume flow**\n\nThis control phase in the warm-up range protects the cylinder head and the turbocharger from overheating from the static coolant in the exhaust manifold. \n\nAt a Rotary valve 1 angle position of 145°, Rotary valve 2 is engaged and begins to open.  A small coolant flow begins through the cylinder block, the cylinder head and the turbocharger returning back to the rotary valve module and coolant pump. \n\nRotary valve 1 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ns522_093 \n\n42",
