    "text": "### **Transmission Coolant Valve N488**\n\nN488 controls the flow of warm coolant from the engine to the transmission gear oil cooler. \n\nWhen required, the solenoid valve is activated by the ECM. \n\nIt is held open by mechanical spring force when not activated and closes when the engine is started. The coolant flow to the transmission opens at a coolant temperature of 176 °F (80 °C)  and closes again at 194 °F (90 °C). This helps the manual transmission to attain its optimal friction temperature. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nElectrical connection\nCoolant flow to the engine\nSolenoid coil\n606_022\nPiston Coolant flow\nto the cooler\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n47",
