    "text": "## **Intake manifold**\n\nTo accommodate both FSI and MPI fuel injectors, a newly designed intake manifold was required.  The manifold also has pan-shaped flaps to direct air flow in the intake duct. An angled, single piece stainless steel shaft maximizes the torsional rigidity of the flaps. At initial launch of these engines, the North American version will only have FSI injection. \n\nThe shaft is actuated by Intake Manifold Runner Control Valve N316 using a vacuum motor based on signals from the ECM. \n\nThe pan-shaped flaps are tensioned in the manifold in such a way to minimize excitation by the airflow. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nFuel Metering Valve N290 Intake Air Temperature Sensor\nG42 with Manifold Absolute\nPressure Sensor G71\nHigh pressure pump\nVacuum motor for intake manifold flaps MPI injectors\nIntake Manifold Runner\nPosition Sensor G336\n606_041\nIntake manifold flaps\nThrottle Valve Control Module J338\nIntake Manifold Runner Control Valve\nN316\n606_042\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n52",
