    "text": "#### **Charge Pressure Actuator Position Sensor G581**\n\nG581 is installed in the charge pressure actuator gear housing cover. A magnetic holder with two permanent magnets is also integrated into the housing cover and rests on the spring seat of the gear. It therefore performs the same movement as the push rod. When the push rod moves, the magnets travel past a Hall sensor also located in the housing cover.  This allows actual adjustment travel to be measured.  The signal from the Hall sensor is an analog, linear voltage signal. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nMagnetic holder\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n\n\nCharge Pressure Actuator Position Sensor G581 \n\n606_079 \n\n55",
