    "page_end": 22,
    "text": "# **Traction control systems**\n\n###### **Vehicle without YMC**\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nS374_065\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nThe side of the vehicle on the surface with better grip is braked more extensively than the side of the vehicle on the smooth surface. The yawing moment which occurs in this case causes a yaw rate, which the driver cannot compensate quickly enough via the steering.\n\n###### **Vehicle with YMC**\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nS374_067\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nThe brake pressure at the wheels on the surface with better grip does not increase so quickly. The dangerous yaw rate is overcome.\n\n##### **How it works**\n\nIf the ABS control system within the YMC function ascertains during a braking manoeuvre that the wheel speeds of the wheels on the left-hand side deviate from those on the right-hand side, the system concludes that disturbing yawing moment may develop. \n\nBraking the wheels with the higher speed is therefore delayed slightly until the wheel speeds on the right- and left-hand sides match each other again. To achieve this, the relevant ABS inlet valves are opened slightly later by the control system, with the result that pressure buildup at the wheel brake cylinder takes place more slowly. \n\n22",
