    "text": "# **Traction control systems**\n\n##### **Pressure maintenance**\n\nTo maintain the brake pressure in the wheel's brake circuit, only the return flow pump is deactivated. The switch valve remains closed. A constant brake pressure is maintained at the wheel brake. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nEDL regulation 1\n\"maintain pressure\"\n26- High-pressure valve 26\n18 S374_324\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n##### **Pressure reduction**\n\nTo reduce pressure, the inlet valve and the switch valve are currentless, i.e. opened. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nEDL regulation 1\n\"reduce pressure\"\n25- Switch valve 6\n26- High-pressure valve 26\n18 S374_326\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n30",
