    "text": "# **Auxiliary ESP functions**\n\n##### **Phase 1: Start of brake assist system intervention**\n\nThe brake assist system increases the brake pressure. Due to this active pressure build-up, the ABS regulation limit is very quickly reached, thereby triggering ABS regulation. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nPhase 1\nS374_182 t[s]\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n\n\nBrake pressure at the wheel brake cylinder Driver's pedal pressure \n\nIn the hydraulic unit, the switch valve is closed and the high-pressure valve is opened. The return flow pump is actuated and begins pumping. As a result of this, the pressure at the wheel brake is increased to the maximum, over and above the brake pressure triggered by the driver. If the wheels are in danger of locking up, ABS intervenes. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nActive pressure build-up 1\n26- High-pressure valve 25\n18 S374_342\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n50\n\n**Phase 2: ABS intervention** \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nPhase 2\nMaintain Build-up\nrange.\nReduce\nS374_188 t[s]\nBrake pressure at the wheel brake cylinder\nDriver's pedal pressure\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nABS intervention keeps the brake pressure below the lock up threshold. Regulation takes place in three phases: \"Maintain pressure\", \"reduce pressure\" and \"build up pressure\". \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\n1 Pressure maintenance\n2 2 - Brake servo\n6 26- High-pressure valve\n18 S374_344\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nTo maintain the brake pressure in the wheel's brake circuit, the inlet valve and the high-pressure valve are closed. A constant brake pressure is maintained at the wheel brake. The return flow pump is deactivated. \n\n51",
