    "text": "# **Assist systems**\n\n##### **Phase 2 – maintain pressure**\n\nThe vehicle is stationary. The driver removes his foot from the brake in order to actuate the accelerator. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nS374_156\nS374_164\nPhase 1 Phase 2 Phase 3 Phase 4\nBraking torque\nS374_148 t[s]\n1 - Reservoir 1\n18 S374_352\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nThe hill start assist system keeps the brake pressure at the wheel brake cylinders constant for approx. 2 seconds to prevent it from rolling backwards. \n\nThe brake pedal is no longer actuated. The switch valve is closed. The pressure is maintained at the wheel brake. This prevents premature pressure reduction. \n\n66\n\n##### **Phase 3 – relieve pressure**\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nS374_158\nS374_164\nPhase 1 Phase 2 Phase 3 Phase 4\nS374_150 t[s]\n18 S374_354\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nThe vehicle is still stationary. The driver actuates the accelerator pedal. \n\nWhilst the driver is increasing the drive torque, the hill start assist system HHC reduces the brake pressure just enough so that the vehicle does not roll backwards and is not restrained when subsequently starting off. \n\nBraking torque Drive torque \n\n\n\nThe switch valve is opened gradually. Due to the open inlet valve, pressure can be reduced at the wheel brake. \n\n67",
