    "text": "## **Front assist system**\n\nThe front assist system is an assist system with a warning function, and serves to prevent rear-end collisions. Stopping distance reduction AWV1 and stopping distance reduction AWV2 form part of the front assist system. When a preceding vehicle is approached in a hazardous manner, the front assist system has two action time points, the preliminary warning and the main warning. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nS374_219\nMain warning\nAWV2: Warning jolt\nAWV1: HBA changeover \"maximum sensitivity\"\nPreliminary warning\nAWV2: Optical/acoustic warning\nAWV1: Prefill\nAWV1: HBA changeover \"increased sensitivity\"\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n##### **Preliminary warning**\n\n##### **Main warning**\n\nIn the event of the preliminary warning, a warning symbol first appears in the dash panel insert (optionally, an acoustic signal is sounded). At the same time, the brake system is pre-filled (Prefill) and the hydraulic brake assist system (HBA) is switched to \"increased sensitivity\". \n\nIf the driver does not react, a brief warning jolt is output. At the same time, the brake assist system is switched to \"maximum sensitivity\". \n\nStopping distance reduction does not take place at a vehicle speed of less than 30 km/h. \n\n80",
