    "page_start": 1,
    "page_end": 2,
    "text": "# The Heat Pump from Volkswagen Design and function olkswlkswkswswwagenAGdo\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nDesign and function\nagenAG.VolkswlkswkswswwagenAGdo\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nHeat pump technology has been used in buildings for many years. At Volkswagen, this efficient technology is being used for the first time to produce heat in the e-Golf. \n\nThe heat pump system is a refrigerant circuit that is made up of numerous components. We will henceforth call it heat pump for short. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nIn cars with an internal combustion engine, the heat produced by the engine can be used to heat the passenger\ncompartment. Electrically driven vehicles, however, do not produce enough thermal energy to heat the vehicle\ninterior.\nUsing a heat pump allows the heat from the outside air and the heat produced by the drive components to be\nemployed to heat the vehicle interior. As a result, less battery power is required by the electrical high-voltage\nheater. The energy consumption is reduced. The range of the e-Golf with a heat pump is increased by over 30\npercent compared with an e-Golf without a heat pump.\ns532_006\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nYou will find basic information on air conditioning in Self-study Programme no. 208 “Air Conditioner in the Motor Vehicle”. Self-study Programme no. 530 “The e-Golf” also contains important information. \n\n\n\n\n\n|This Self-study Programme describes|For current testing, adjustment and repair||\n|---|---|---|\n|the design and function of new<br>developments.|instructions, refer to the relevant service<br>literature.|Important|\n|The contents will not be updated..||note|\n\n\n\n2",
