    "page_end": 4,
    "text": "### Phase transition\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nThere are three traditional states of matter or phases The phases of water\nthat substances can change between as a result of\nsimple variations in temperature or pressure: solid,\nFreezing Condensation\nliquid and gas.\nTo change its state of matter, a body must either\nabsorb or release thermal energy:\nMelting Vaporisation\n• Melting: is the transition from solid to liquid state.\nHeat is absorbed in this case. Solid Liquid Gas\n• Vaporisation: is the transition from liquid to\ngaseous state. Heat is absorbed in this case. s532_001\n• Condensation: is the transition from gaseous to\nliquid state. Heat is released in this case.\n• Freezing: is the transition from liquid to solid state.\nHeat is released in this case.\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n4",
