    "text": "#### K: critical point\n\nThe boiling line is to the left of the critical point and the saturated vapour line is to the right of it. \n\n8\n\nThe heat pump in the e-Golf System configuration Components like the electrical air conditioner compressor, the evaporator and the condenser are used to run the air conditioning system in the e-Golf. The refrigerant circuit of the air conditioning system has been expanded for use with the heat pump to include refrigerant lines, electrical expansion valves, pressure senders, temperature senders and a heat condenser. Since the heat pump system for the e-Golf also uses the heat produced by the motor and the power and control electronics for electric drive, a second expansion valve and a heat exchanger for the heat condenser are used in parallel to heat pump circuit. Refrigerant circuit in the vehicle Pressure and temperature senders Expansion/shut-off valves Condenser Electrical air conditioner compressor Heat exchanger for heat condenser Evaporator s532_007 Heat condenser olksw \n\n9\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nThe heat pump in the e-Golf\nSchematic diagram of refrigerant circuit\nThis schematic diagram of the heat pump refrigerant circuit provides a basic illustration for the subsequent\ndescriptions of components and the individual functions of the heat pump.\nV470\nG395\nG829 N642\nReservoir\nN643\nN696\nG827\nG826\nN636\nHeater and air\nconditioning unit\nG828 N637\nN638 Heat condenser\nHeat exchanger for heat Evaporator\nG787 G110\nNon-return valve\nG785\nAX4\nV509\nG931\nN632\nVX54\nG789\nJX1\nV508 G788\nG83\nN687\ns532_090\nRadiator\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n10",
