    "text": "### Fitting location\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nElectrical air conditioner compressor\nThe electrical air conditioner compressor V470 is\nbolted to the three-phase current drive VX54.\nThe e-Golf with heat pump uses an electrical air\nconditioner compressor that is based on a spiral or\nscroll compressor design.\nIt is identical to the air conditioner compressor fitted in\nthe e-Golf without a heat pump.\ns532_024\nThe electrical air conditioner compressor draws in the\ngaseous refrigerant at low pressure.\nIt is compressed in this compressor.\nThe pressure increases and the temperature of the\nrefrigerant also rises.\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nThe electrical air conditioner compressor pushes the refrigerant to the condenser as a hot gas. This compressor therefore forms the separating point between the low-pressure and high-pressure sides of the refrigerant circuit. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\ns532_021\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nYou will find further information on the design and function of a spiral or scroll compressor in Selfstudy Programme no. 525 “The Jetta Hybrid”. \n\n\n\n12\n\nHeat condenser and evaporator Fitting location of heat condenser/evaporator The heat pump in the e-Golf has a heat condenser and an evaporator. Both are fitted in the heater and air conditioning unit. Evaporator Design of heat condenser The heat condenser consists of a serpentine-like pipe system that is fixed to fins. This creates a large heat Heat condenser exchange area with good heat transfer. A flow of air produced by the heater and air conditioning unit fan s532_026 passes through the heat condenser. olksw\n\n##### Heat condenser\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\ns532_009\n<!-- End of picture text -->",
