    "text": "### Design of expansion valves\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nExpansion valve The expansion valves have an identical design. A V-\nshaped control edge in the ball valve enables on-\ndemand, stepless activation (0-100 percent).\nExpansion valve function\ns532_011\nThe refrigerant can expand in the expansion valve,\ni.e. fill a considerably larger space (volume\nenlargement). The pressure then falls significantly. The\nRefrigerant flows through the expansion\nliquid refrigerant partially evaporates. The\nvalve N637 from the evaporator in the\ntemperature falls as a result.\ndirection of the condenser in “heating”\noperating mode (function).\nIn “cooling” operating mode (function),\nthe refrigerant flows through the\nexpansion valve in the opposite direction.\nDesign of shut-off valves\nShut-off valve The shut-off valves are ball valves that are either fully\nopen or fully closed.\nShut-off valve function\ns532_017\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nThe shut-off valves regulate the flow direction of refrigerant in the refrigerant circuit. \n\nThe expansion valves and shut-off valves are connected to the thermal management control unit J1024 via the same LIN bus. Each compact valve connector has its own coded pin assignment. \n\n\n\n15\n\nComponents",
