    "text": "### Fitting location\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nThe heat exchanger for heat condenser is fitted on an\nassembly carrier that is mounted on the bulkhead in\nthe motor compartment. Most of the heat pump\ncomponents are mounted on it.\nThe heat exchanger for heat condenser is a\nconventional plate heat exchanger as used to cool oil\nHeat exchanger for circuits with coolant.\nThe coolant circuit is separate from the refrigerant\ncircuit. Heat is exchanged without direct contact\nbetween or mixing of the fluids.\ns532_046\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n### Function\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nConnections for\nrefrigerant\nConnections for\ncoolant\ns532_013\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nIn the heat exchanger for heat condenser, the heat of the coolant is transferred to the refrigerant and the refrigerant evaporates. \n\nThe heat from electronic components like, for example, the three-phase current drive, the power and control electronics for electric drive and the charging unit, is used for this purpose. \n\n17\n\nComponents",
