    "text": "### Fitting location\n\nThe reservoir is upstream of the electrical air conditioner compressor in the refrigerant flow direction. \n\nThe reservoir is fitted at the front right in the wheel housing.\n\n### Design\n\nIt is identical to the reservoir in other vehicles with air conditioning. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nReservoir\ns532_034\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n### Function\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nThe reservoir is used in the refrigerant circuit as an Refrigerant outlet Refrigerant\nto electrical air inlet\nexpansion and supply tank for the refrigerant. Since\nconditioner\nthe thermal loading of the evaporator and condenser compressor\nand the speed of the electrical air conditioner\ncompressor will vary during operation, different\nquantities of refrigerant will also be pumped through\nthe circuit.\nThe reservoir is incorporated into the circuit to\ncompensate these fluctuations.\ns532_023\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\ns532_023 \n\n18\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nRefrigerant pressure and temperature senders\nG395\nA total of five refrigerant pressure and temperature\nG829\nsenders are installed in the heat pump circuit.\nThey are located on the assembly carrier:\n• G395 Refrigerant pressure and temperature\nsender\nG827\n• G826 Refrigerant pressure and temperature\nG826\nsender 2\n• G827 Refrigerant pressure and temperature\nsender 3\nG828 • G828 Refrigerant pressure and temperature\nsender 4\n• G829 Refrigerant pressure and temperature\nsender 5\ns532_044\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n### Function\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\ns532_015\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nThe refrigerant pressure and temperature senders measure the pressure and the temperature of the refrigerant, convert the readings into an electrical signal and send it to the heat pump control unit. The following data is collected: \n\n- Refrigerant pressure 0 to 36bar \n\n- Refrigerant temperature minus 40°C to plus 150°C \n\n- Internal temperature sender minus 40°C to plus 140°C\n\n### Effects upon failure\n\nThe refrigerant pressure and temperature senders can only be exchanged after the refrigerant has been extracted. \n\n\n\nIf one or more sensors fail, the refrigerant pressure and the refrigerant temperature are determined using a map. The heating up phase for the vehicle interior is increased and an entry is made in the event memory. \n\n19\n\nComponents",
