    "text": "## Heating function in air mode\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nElectrical air conditioner compressor\ns532_014\nEV2 Key\nThis function uses only the heat from the outside air to heat the vehicle interior.\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n1. The electrical air conditioner compressor compresses the refrigerant. The gaseous refrigerant is under high pressure at a high temperature. \n\n2. In the heat condenser, the refrigerant transfers heat to the air and starts to condense. The heated air flows as heating air into the vehicle interior. \n\n3. Shut-off valves 1 and 4 are closed. The pressure is reduced via expansion valve 1 and the temperature of the liquid refrigerant decreases. \n\n4. The evaporator now works as a condenser. The in-flowing refrigerant condenses and releases heat. The now pre-heated air flows further to the heat condenser. \n\n5. Expansion valve 3 is closed. The refrigerant pressure is lowered further via expansion valve 2. The refrigerant temperature now falls below the ambient temperature. \n\n6. The cold refrigerant, which is below ambient temperature, evaporates in the condenser. The heat of vaporisation required for this process is drawn from the warmer outside air, which then cools down. The gaseous refrigerant leaves the condenser and flows through the open shut-off valve 5 in the direction of the air conditioner compressor. \n\n22\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nPhase diagram of the R134a refrigerant\nThe following diagram shows the state of the R134a refrigerant during the heating function (air mode).\ns532_016\nEnergy content (kJ/kg)\n<!-- End of picture text -->",
