    "text": "### Sleep and wake-up modes of the data bus systems\n\nWhen all of the control units of the convenience and infotainment CAN data bus have announced their readiness for stand-by, a control unit will give the signal to 'sleep'. The voltage level of the low signal is 12 V and 0 V for the high signal. \n\nFurthermore, it also gives the wake-up signal when the data bus has to be activated, for example, when the doors are unlocked. \n\nThe data bus diagnosis interface monitors the sleep function. \n\nIf the drive train CAN data bus does not go into sleep mode, the convenience and infotainment CAN data buses do not go into sleep mode either. \n\nIf the convenience CAN data bus does not go into sleep mode, the infotainment CAN data bus does not go into sleep mode either. \n\n\n\n\n\nS307_048 \n\nSleep mode \n\nWake-up signal \n\nWake-up mode \n\n27\n\nOnboard power supply control unit",
