    "text": "### Windscreen wiper motor actuation\n\nThe wiper system consists of a twin motor opposing action system without a mechanical connection between the wiper arms. \n\nInformation about the selected wiper stage is sent from the onboard power supply control unit via the LIN data bus to the wiper motor control unit J400 and from there to the wiper control unit, front passenger side J584. \n\nThe switch position of wiper switch E is sent directly to the steering column electronics control unit J527 and then via the convenience CAN data bus to the onboard power supply control unit J519. \n\nBoth control units are located directly on the wiper motors. \n\nThe wiper motor control unit J400 manages control of the wiper motion and regulates the wiper control unit, front passenger side J584.",
