    "text": "### Anti-blocking function\n\nThe wiper system detects if the wipers are blokked by the amount of current that is drawn. If there is a blockage in area A, it will attempt to remove this a total of five times. If it is unable to move the blockage, the wipers will remain in the rest position. The blockage will have to be removed manually. \n\nIf the wiper blades are frozen to the bottom part of the windscreen, the wipers will attempt to break free a total of five times. After the fifth attempt, there will be no wiper motion. \n\n\n\nS307_033",
