    "text": "#### Clutch and brake application in 8-speed gearbox 09S\n\nApplication of clutches and brakes according to the gear engaged is shown below. \n\n|Drive||||Components||||\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n||K1|K2|K3|K4|B1|B2|F|\n|I|•|-|-|-|-|•|•|\n|II|•|-|-|-|•|-|-|\n|III|•|-|•|-|-|-|-|\n|IV|•|-|-|•|-|-|-|\n|V|•|•|-|-|-|-|-|\n|VI|-|•|-|•|-|-|-|\n|VII|-|•|•|-|-|-|-|\n|VIII|-|•|-|-|•|-|-|\n|Reverse|-|-|•|-|-|•|-|\n\n\n\n\n\n- applied \n\n- not applied \n\nWhere: \n\n- Letter “K” designates the different multi-disk clutches (from 1 to 4) \n\n- Term B1 designates the multi-disc brake 1. \n\n- Term B2 designates the multi-disc brake 2. \n\n- Letter F designates the freewheeling mechanism. \n\nEngine brake: the engine braking effect is achieved by selecting first gear in Tiptronic mode in order to control specific driving situations such as driving downhill. \n\nThe multi-disc brake B2 only operates in first gear with Tiptronic mode on. This mode is also known as manual first gear. \n\n29\n\nRunning Gear",
