    "text": "#### Readiness Code\n\n8-digit binary code which indicates whether all diagnoses affecting exhaust emissions have been conducted by the engine management system. The Readiness Code is generated when: \n\nA fault is indicated in the form of a steady or a flashing light after it is detected by the control unit either \n\n- immediately or \n\n- after 2 driving cycles depending on the nature of the fault and what display conditions apply. \n\nThere are also faults which are stored to memory but which do not activate the self-diagnosis fault warning lamp (MIL). \n\n- all diagnoses have been conducted without fault and the self-diagnosis fault warning lamp (MIL) is not lit, \n\n- all diagnoses have been conducted, detected faults have been stored to fault memory and indicated by the self-diagnosis fault warning lamp (MIL). \n\n10\n\nOBD-II Diagnosis Stored malfunctions can be exported by means Lawmakers have stipulated that diagnosis of a Scan Tool connected to the diagnosis intersystems must be designed by auto makers in such face which can be accessed from the driver's a way that OBD data can be interrogated with seat. any OBD reader (Generic Scan Tool). In the new program version, the diagnosis with This Generic Scan Tool mode can be invoked by VAG 1551 offers the following possibilities: diagnosis systems V.A.G 1551 (software version 5.0 or higher), G Read out/erase fault memory V.A.G 1552 (software version 2.0 or higher) and G Display data relevant to assemblies to support VAS 5051 via address word \"33“. troubleshooting However, the units can also provide - via address G Read Readiness Codes word \"01“ - functions which go far beyond this G Execute a short trip mode and are required for troubleshooting and (to generate the Readiness Codes) repair work as well as reading and generating G Print diagnosis data Readiness Codes. olksw \n\n\n\n175_006 \n\n\n\n175_007 \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\n175_010\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n11\n\nOverview of OBD-II (Gasoline Engine)",
