    "text": "#### Catalytic conversion diagnosis\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nDuring the diagnosis, the Motronic control unit The engine management system interprets any\ncompares the voltages of the primary and deviation from the nominal range as a mal-\nsecondary catalytic converter probes. It deter- functioning of the catalytic converter.\nmines what is known as the primary to secondary After meeting the fault conditions, the fault code\ncatalytic converter ratio (lambda probes I+II). is saved to fault memory.\nThe fault is indicated by the self-diagnosis fault\nwarning lamp (MIL).\nCatalytic converter Catalytic converter\n175_041 175_042\nU U U U\nt t t t\nPrimary catalytic Secondary Primary catalytic Secondary\nconverter catalytic converter converter catalytic converter\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nV = voltage, t = time \n\n24\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nHazards to the catalytic converter\nAs a result of the prevailing temperature condi- For example, if misfiring occurs in the catalytic\ntions, catalytic converters are subjected to an converter during operation as a result of high\naging process that affects their conversion temperatures, the active catalyst surface may\ncharacteristics. become damaged.\nIn addition to this thermal aging process, the Mechanical damage to the catalytic converter is\nconversion characteristics of the catalytic con- also possible.\nverter may also be impaired by poisoning\n(chemical aging).\nEmission limits for gasoline vehicles\nTwo examples of the currently valid limit values are shown here. However, these values cannot be com-\npared with one another because different test methods are used.\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n\n\n- G The limit values for passenger cars which are approved for max. 12 persons applicable in the U.S. Federal State of California with effect from model year 1999. \n\n- G The limit values currently in force in the Federal Republic of Germany comply with the D3 standard. \n\nThe limit values conform to the LEV approval level. \n\n|Pollutant|Durability<br>[mi]|Limit value<br>MY ‘99<br>[g/mi]|\n|---|---|---|\n|NMOG|50,000|0.075|\n||100,000|0.09|\n|CO|50,000|3.4|\n||100,000|4.2|\n|NOx|50,000|0.2|\n||100,000|0.3|\n\n\n\nNMOG (Non-Methane Organic Gases) is the sum of all oxygen-containing and oxygen-free hydrocarbons in the exhaust gas. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\ng/km\n2.4\n2.2\n2.0\n1.8\n1.6 1.50\n0.17\n175_043 0.2 0.14\nCO HC NOx\n175_155\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n25\n\nSystem Components (Gasoline Engine)",
