    "text": "### The lambda probe\n\nThe lambda probe measures the oxygen component in the exhaust gas mixture. It is an integral part of a closed control loop which maintains the correct composition of the air-fuel mixture. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nintegral part of a closed control loop which\nmaintains the correct composition of the air-fuel\nmixture.\nThe air-oxygen-to-fuel mixing ratio at which\nmaximum conversion of the pollutants takes\nplace in the catalytic converter is λ =1\n(stoichiometric mixing ratio). 175_045\nChanges in exhaust gas composition are com-\npensated for by the engine management system\nwhen it controls a number of functions and often\nserve as an early indication of a possible fault.\nDisturbances\nG Mechanical faults G Aging\nG Electrical faults G Driving influences\n175_046\nMotronic control unit Injection quantity Enriched Little O2 in exhaust gas\nenriches mixture increased mixture\nLambda probe Lambda probe\nsignal change U voltage high\nLambda probe Lambda probe\nvoltage low signal change\nHigh O2 concentration in Lean Injection quantity Motronic control unit\nexhaust gas mixture reduced enleans the mixture\nRich mixture λ≈ 1 (lambda window) Lean mixture\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n26",
