    "text": "#### Effects of signal failure\n\nIf the lambda probe signal fails, lambda control does not take place and the lambda adaption function is disabled. \n\n\n\n\n\nThe tank ventilation system goes to emergency mode. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nmode.\nThe Motronic control unit uses a map-based\nopen control loop as an emergency function.\nG39\n175_055\nLambda probe G108\nis the secondary catalytic converter probe.\n175_056\nEffects of signal failure\nThe engine lambda control remains operational Electrical circuit\neven if the secondary catalytic converter probe\nfails. Only the function of the catalytic converter\ncan no longer be checked if the probe fails.\nIn the Motronic M5.9.2, the function test on the\nprimary catalytic converter probe no longer\ntakes place.\nG108\n175_055\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n30",
