    "text": "#### <mark>Diagnosis of a minor leak</mark>\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nThe test phase starts after the fuel system The larger the leak, the quicker the succession of\ndiagnosis pump in the tank system has built up diagnosis pump delivery periods. This indicates a\nan overpressure. The drop in overpressure is possible leak and the size of this leak.\nmonitored at the same time.\nA reed switch is coupled with a membrane in the\nfuel system diagnosis pump.\nIf the pressure in the tank system drops, the posi-\ntion of the membrane changes. If the pressure\ndrops below a defined value, the reed switch\ncloses and the pump increases the pressure\nagain until the reed switch is reopened by the\nmembrane.\nTank system Tank system\ntight minor leak\nP P\nLeak\n175_086 175_087\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nP = pressure, t = time \n\n40\n\nDiagnosis of a major leak If the frequency of the delivery periods exceeds a certain value, or if the pump fails to build up the necessary pressure, the engine management system concludes that a major leak has occurred. For example, this fault message can also be caused by forgetting to fit the fuel filler cap. olksw \n\n\n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nTank system Tank system\ntight major leak\nP P\nLeak\n175_086 175_089\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n41\n\nSystem Components (Gasoline Engine)",
