    "text": "#### Fuel system diagnosis pump V144\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\n175_171\nThe fuel system diagnosis pump takes the form of The reed switch monitors the measurement\na diaphragm pump. It is mounted at the ventila- sequence of the diagnosis pump.\ntion connection of the activated charcoal canister If the pressure inside the tank system drops\n(ACF) and contains an integrated ACF shut-off below a defined value, the reed switch closes\nvalve. The fuel system diagnosis pump is driven and the pump executes another diaphragm\nby the intake pipe vacuum via an internal stroke causing the switch to reopen.\nvacuum switch.\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nThe diagnosis pump is activated after the cold start. This disables the fuel tank purging system function until the end of the leak diagnosis cycle. \n\n\n\nThe tank level does not affect the outcome of the diagnosis. \n\n42\n\n#### Function",
