    "text": "#### Engine speed sender G28\n\nThis inductive sender detects crankshaft rpm data and makes it possible to monitor the running characteristics of the engine. \n\nThe signal generated by the sensors is used to calculate: \n\n- the fuel injection quantity and point, \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\n175_099\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n- the ignition point, and \n\n- engine speed. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nEffects of signal failure\nIf the engine speed signal fails, the engine can-\nnot be started.\nIf the fault occurs when the engine is running, the\nengine cuts out.\nG28 175_100\nHall sender G40\nThe signal generated by the Hall sender helps to\ndetect cylinder 1.\nIn the New Beetle (U.S.A.), the Hall sender is\ndesigned as a camshaft sensor.\n175_101\nEffects of signal failure\nMisfire detection is also possible if sensor G40\nfails. For engine operation, the system retards the\nignition advance angle as an emergency\nfunction.\n<!-- End of picture text -->",
