    "text": "#### Knock sensors G61 and G66\n\nElectronic control of the ignition point is superimposed on cylinder-selective knock control. Cylinder-selective assignment of knock signals is by means of the Hall sender which recognizes the first cylinder and the position of the crankshaft. \n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\ncontrol. Cylinder-selective assignment of knock\nsignals is by means of the Hall sender which\nrecognizes the first cylinder and the position of\nthe crankshaft.\n175_137\nAfter a knocking cylinder is detected, the ignition\nadvance angle of the cylinder in question is\nretarded incrementally until knocking is Electrical circuit\neliminated.\nEffects of signal failure\nIf G61 fails, the ignition advance angle for all\ncylinders is retarded and the mixture is enriched.\nG61 G66\n175_138\nInjectors N30, N31, N32, N33\nThe injectors with vertical fuel feed are secured\nto a common fuel manifold by means of securing\nclip.\n175_143\nPower is supplied by a thermal trip.\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nN30 N31 N32 N33\n+ 175_144\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n56",
