    "text": "#### Speedometer sender G22\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nSpeedometer sender G22\nThe installation position of the speedometer\nsender is on the transmission housing. It records\nthe vehicle road speed.\nEffects of signal failure\n175_145\nIf the signal fails, the speed limiting device cuts in\nearly. Electrical circuit\nThis may cause the driver problems in handling\nthe vehicle.\nJ285\nG22\n175_146\nCoolant temperature sender G62\nThe coolant temperature sender is located in the\ncoolant outlet hose at the cylinder head.\nIts signal also influences a wide range of\nfunctions of the ignition and injection systems.\nEffects of signal failure 175_149\nior o\nup fo\nlia fni\ncre ro\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\nIf G62 fails, the system computes a substitute value from the intake pipe temperature and other engine operating conditions. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nG62\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\n175_150\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n58\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nNotes\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n59\n\nOverview of OBD-II (Diesel)",
