    "text": "#### Summary: Readiness Code/short trip\n\nThe Readiness Code contains no information on After the mechanic eliminates the fault, he clears whether faults exist in the system. It only indicates the fault memory. This resets the Readiness Code. whether certain diagnoses have been completed For the engine management system, this means (bit to 0) or have not been carried out yet or that all diagnoses have to be repeated. have been aborted (bit to 1). The short trip was created for workshops, since If one or more faults is detected and stored, some diagnosis conditions are difficult to fulfill illumination of the self-diagnosis fault warning during normal vehicle operation. The short trip lamp (MIL) is the only visual indication to the makes it possible for workshops to carry out driver or inspecting police officer. diagnoses selectively under the appropriate conditions in order to recreate the Readiness Code If the engine management system detects a fault relatively quickly. and stores a corresponding fault message to the fault memory in accordance with the applicable storage conditions, the fault can only be detected with a Scan-ool or V.A.G Tester by reading out the fault memory. olksw \n\n\n\n\n\nMake sure you do not accidentally erase the fault memory or disconnect the Motronic control unit from the power supply because this will cancel the Readiness Code and you will have to create a new Readiness Code. \n\n82",
