    "text": "#### Diagnosis for diesel vehicles (TDI)\n\nThe diesel direct injection system control unit (EDC 15V) is also equipped with a fault memory. After entering a fault, this can be displayed in two ways:\n\n##### Glow period warning lamp\n\nSelf-diagnosis fault warning lamp (MIL) \n\n- Faults which affect exhaust emission quality are indicated by the self-diagnosis fault warning lamp (MIL). These faults are recorded during the course of the OBD-II diagnosis. \n\n- Faults which affect handling performance and driving safety are indicated by flashing of the glow period warning lamp. \n\ndriving safety are indicated by flashing of the glow period warning lamp. 175_165 If a fault is stored, it can be read out with diagnosis systems V.A.G 1551/1552 and VAS 505. Reading out and generating the Readiness Code In the New Beetle (U.S.A) with OBD-II (diesel), Readiness Code generation does not have to be the procedure for reading out and generating initiated by means of the diagnosis system. The the Readiness Code differs from the procedure Readiness code can be generated by conducting for the gasoline engine. a defined test routine when the vehicle is stationary. The fault memory can be read out via - Address word “01” Engine electronics, - Function “08” Read measured value block and olksw \n\n\n\n- Display Group “17” Readiness Code. \n\n\n\nYou can find a breakdown and procedure for generating Readiness Codes for the diesel engine in the relevant Workshop Manual. \n\n83\n\nFunction Diagram (2.0-Liter Gasoline Engine) \n\n\n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nV144 G88 G69 F60 V60\nN112 N30 N31 N32 N33\nV101\nN80 G70 G39 G108\n175_169a\nComponents G70 Air-mass flow meter\nG88 Throttle valve positioner potentiometer\nF60 Idling speed switch G108 Lambda probe II\nG28 Engine speed sender J220 Motronic control unit\nG39 Lambda probe I J299 Secondary air pump relay\nG40 Hall sender J338 Throttle valve control unit\nG61 Knock sensor I\nG62 Coolant temperature sender\nG66 Knock sensor II\nG69 Throttle valve potentiometer\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n84\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nN152\nA B C\nInput signal\nOutput signal\nPositive\nGround\nData line\nG61 G66 G62 G40 K83\n175_169b\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n- N30 Injector, cylinder 1 V60 N31 Injector, cylinder 2 V101 N32 Injector, cylinder 3 V144 N33 Injector, cylinder 4 N80 Activated charcoal filter system solenoid valve 1 A N112 Secondary air inlet valve N152 Ignition transformer B S Fuse C CAN bus \n\n   - V60 Throttle valve positioner V101 Secondary air pump motor V144 Fuel system diagnosis pump \n\n   - A Signal to self-diagnosis fault warning lamp K83 (via CAN bus from model year 2000) \n\n   - B Road speed signal from control unit with display unit in dash panel insert J285 \n\n\n\n85\n\nFunction Diagram (1.9-Liter TDI) \n\n\n\n\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nN18 N75 N108 G70\nJ248\nJ52 N146\nG81 G149\nQ6\n175_170a\nComponents G80 Needle lift sender\nG81 Fuel temperature sender\nF8 Kick-down switch G149 Modulating piston movement sender\nF60 Idling speed switch in G79\nJ52 Glow plug relay\nG28 Engine speed sender J248 Diesel direct injection system control unit\nG62 Coolant temperature sender\nG70 Air-mass flow meter\nG71 Intake manifold pressure sender\nG72 Intake manifold temperature sensor\nG79 Accelerator position sender\n<!-- End of picture text -->\n\n86\n\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\nG28 G80\nA B C D\nInput signal\nOutput signal\nJ248\nPositive\nGround\nData line\nG62 G71 G72 F60 F8 G79\n175_170b\nN18 Exhaust gas recirculation valve A CAN bus\nN75 Charge pressure control solenoid valve B Road speed signal from control unit\nN108 Commencement of injection valve with display unit in dash panel insert J285\nN146 Quantity adjuster C Signal to glow period warning lamp K29\n(via CAN bus from model year 2000)\nQ6 Glow plugs (engine) D Signal to self-diagnosis fault warning lamp K83\n(via CAN bus from model year 2000)\nS Fuse\n<!-- End of picture text -->\